{"id": "a-project-is-written-as-files", "category": "files", "turns": ["create a python project: a hello world fastapi"], "script": ["<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp/main.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Run it with `uvicorn app.main:app`."], "expect": {"route": {"tool": "write_file", "via": "model"}, "calls": ["write_file"], "max_model_passes": 2}}
{"id": "a-project-asked-for-then-described", "category": "files", "turns": ["I want to create a python project", "first init a new basic hello world fastapi"], "script": ["What should it do?", "<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp/main.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Run it with `uvicorn app.main:app`."], "expect": {"calls": ["write_file"]}}
{"id": "code-shown-then-written-as-files", "category": "files", "turns": ["show me a hello world fastapi app", "can you create the files and write to them"], "script": ["```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\napp = FastAPI()\n```", "<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp/main.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Run it with `uvicorn app.main:app`."], "expect": {"calls": ["write_file"]}}
{"id": "a-question-about-code-is-answered-not-filed", "category": "files", "turns": ["what does a python decorator do"], "script": ["It wraps a function in another one."], "expect": {"route": {"tool": null, "via": "model"}}}
{"id": "a-change-edits-only-that-file", "category": "files", "turns": ["create a hello world fastapi project", "add a /health route"], "script": ["<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp/main.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n\n@app.get(\"/\")\ndef root():\n    return {\"message\": \"Hello, World!\"}\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\nrequirements.txt\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\nfastapi\nuvicorn\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Created. Run it with `uvicorn app.main:app`.", "<tool_call>\n<function=edit_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp/main.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=old_string>\n@app.get(\"/\")\ndef root():\n    return {\"message\": \"Hello, World!\"}\n</parameter>\n<parameter=new_string>\n@app.get(\"/\")\ndef root():\n    return {\"message\": \"Hello, World!\"}\n\n\n@app.get(\"/health\")\ndef health():\n    return {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Added a /health route."], "expect": {"calls": ["edit_file"], "max_model_passes": 2, "file_contains": {"app/main.py": ["/health", "Hello, World!"], "requirements.txt": ["fastapi"]}, "prompt_contains": ["Project files: app/main.py (", "requirements.txt ("]}}
{"id": "an-unchanged-file-is-not-written-again", "category": "files", "turns": ["create hello.py that prints hello", "make it say hello world"], "script": ["<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\nhello.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\nprint(\"hello\")\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Created hello.py.", "<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\nhello.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\nprint(\"hello\")\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "<tool_call>\n<function=edit_file>\n<parameter=path>\nhello.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=old_string>\nprint(\"hello\")\n</parameter>\n<parameter=new_string>\nprint(\"hello world\")\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "It prints hello world now."], "scripted_only": true, "expect": {"calls": ["write_file", "edit_file"], "file_contains": {"hello.py": ["hello world"]}, "prompt_contains": ["hello.py already has exactly this content, so nothing was saved"]}}
{"id": "a-pasted-error-is-fixed-where-it-is", "category": "files", "turns": ["write app.py that prints the total of 1, 2 and 3", "I ran it and got:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"app.py\", line 2, in <module>\n    print(totl)\nNameError: name 'totl' is not defined"], "script": ["<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\ntotal = sum([1, 2, 3])\nprint(totl)\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Written.", "Line 2 prints `totl`, a misspelling of `total`.\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=edit_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=old_string>\nprint(totl)\n</parameter>\n<parameter=new_string>\nprint(total)\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Fixed: it prints 6 now."], "expect": {"calls": ["edit_file"], "max_model_passes": 2, "file_contains": {"app.py": ["print(total)"]}, "answer_contains": ["totl"]}}
{"id": "an-edit-that-does-not-match-is-sent-back", "category": "files", "turns": ["write app.py that prints the total of 1, 2 and 3", "rename totl to total"], "script": ["<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\ntotal = sum([1, 2, 3])\nprint(totl)\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Written.", "<tool_call>\n<function=edit_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=old_string>\nprint( totl )\n</parameter>\n<parameter=new_string>\nprint(total)\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "<tool_call>\n<function=read_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp.py\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "<tool_call>\n<function=edit_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=old_string>\nprint(totl)\n</parameter>\n<parameter=new_string>\nprint(total)\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Renamed."], "scripted_only": true, "expect": {"calls": ["edit_file", "read_file", "edit_file"], "file_contains": {"app.py": ["print(total)"]}, "prompt_contains": ["old_string was not found in app.py", "2│ print(totl)"]}}
{"id": "a-run-error-reaches-the-model-whole", "category": "files", "turns": ["write app.py that prints the total of 1, 2 and 3", "run it"], "tools": {"run_file": "run_file_name_error.json"}, "script": ["<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\ntotal = sum([1, 2, 3])\nprint(totl)\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Written.", "<tool_call>\n<function=run_file>\n<parameter=path>\napp.py\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "It stopped: line 2 uses `totl`, which is not defined."], "scripted_only": true, "expect": {"calls": ["run_file"], "prompt_contains": ["exited with code 1", "NameError: name 'totl' is not defined"]}}
{"id": "a-file-is-moved-into-a-folder", "category": "files", "turns": ["create main.py that prints hi", "move main.py into an app folder"], "script": ["<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\nmain.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\nprint('hi')\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Created main.py.", "<tool_call>\n<function=move_file>\n<parameter=source>\nmain.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=destination>\napp/\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "It is app/main.py now."], "expect": {"calls": ["move_file"], "max_model_passes": 2, "file_contains": {"app/main.py": ["print('hi')"]}, "files_absent": ["main.py"], "prompt_contains": ["Moved main.py to app/main.py."]}}
{"id": "a-folder-is-renamed", "category": "files", "turns": ["create src/a.py and src/b.py", "rename the src folder to app"], "script": ["<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\nsrc/a.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\na = 1\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\nsrc/b.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\nb = 2\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Created both.", "<tool_call>\n<function=move_file>\n<parameter=source>\nsrc\n</parameter>\n<parameter=destination>\napp\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Renamed src to app."], "expect": {"calls": ["move_file"], "max_model_passes": 2, "file_contains": {"app/a.py": ["a = 1"], "app/b.py": ["b = 2"]}, "files_absent": ["src/a.py", "src/b.py"], "prompt_contains": ["Moved 2 files from src/ to app/."]}}
{"id": "a-deleted-file-is-gone-from-the-next-turn", "category": "files", "turns": ["create main.py and old.py", "delete old.py", "which files are there now?"], "script": ["<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\nmain.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\nprint(1)\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\nold.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\nx = 1\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Created both.", "<tool_call>\n<function=delete_file>\n<parameter=path>\nold.py\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Deleted old.py.", "Only main.py."], "expect": {"calls": [], "max_model_passes": 1, "files_absent": ["old.py"], "file_contains": {"main.py": ["print(1)"]}, "prompt_contains": ["Deleted old.py.", "Project files: main.py (1 line, v1)."]}}
{"id": "a-move-onto-a-file-is-refused", "category": "files", "turns": ["create a.py and b.py", "move a.py to b.py"], "script": ["<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\na.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\na = 1\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "<tool_call>\n<function=write_file>\n<parameter=path>\nb.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=content>\nb = 2\n\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "Created both.", "<tool_call>\n<function=move_file>\n<parameter=source>\na.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=destination>\nb.py\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "b.py is there already, so I left both as they are."], "scripted_only": true, "expect": {"calls": ["move_file"], "file_contains": {"a.py": ["a = 1"], "b.py": ["b = 2"]}, "prompt_contains": ["Nothing was moved: there is a file there already: b.py."]}}
